[167.585649, "o", "     if not line:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                         raise RuntimeError(\"committed shard truncated: %s\" % name)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                     remaining -= len(line)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                     if line.strip():\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                         yield json.loads(line)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         return\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     for path in shard_paths(index_dir):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>             for line in fh:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                 if line.strip():\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                     yield json.loads(line)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ''' +s[b:]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> open(p,'w').write(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p='reindex/worker.py'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> s=open(p).read().replace('    rows = list(iter_rows(args.index_dir)) if Path(args.index_dir).exists() else []', '    rows = list(iter_rows(args.index_dir, state[\"shards\"]))').replace('    print(\"index      : %d rows, %d unique ids (%.1f%% of source)\"', '"]
[167.585655, "o", "    print(\"index      : %d rows, %d unique ids (%.1f%% of source, committed)\"')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> open(p,'w').write(s)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p='tests/test_durability.py'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> s=open(p).read().replace('import json\\n', 'import io\\nimport json\\n').replace('from reindex.source import Doc, SCHEMA', 'from reindex.source import SCHEMA').replace('from reindex.worker import parse_args, run', 'from reindex.worker import parse_args, run, show_status')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> a=s.index('    def test_every_rotated_shard')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> s=s[:a]+'''    def test_status_ignores_uncommitted_torn_tail_without_mutating_it(self):\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         run(self.args)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         tail = shard_paths(self.index)[-1]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         with tail.op"]
[167.590188, "i", "en('ab') as fh:\n            fh.write(b'{\"id\":999,\"text\":\"caf\\\\xc3')\n        before = tail.read_bytes()\n        with mock.patch('sys.stdout', new_callable=io.StringIO) as output:\n            show_status(self.args)\n        self.assertIn('33 rows, 33 unique ids', output.getvalue())\n        self.assertEqual(tail.read_bytes(), before)\n        run(self.args)  # Even a complete checkpoint recovers uncommitted tails.\n        self.assert_complete()\n\n''' + s[a:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Restart / durability protocol\n\nKeep invoking `./jobs reindex` until it exits 0 (75 means the supervised budget\nexpired; committed work is safe). `./jobs status` reports checkpoint-certified\nrows, excluding any uncommitted tail. `./jobs history` records supervised runs.\nThe usual budget, grace period, cooldown, and supervisor locking are unchanged.\n\nEach batch (or partial batch on SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP) is committed in this order:\n\n1. Flush rows, fsync **every** touched shard (including rotated ones), and sync"]
[167.590207, "i", "\n   the index directory.\n2. Write the new checkpoint to a temporary file, fsync it, atomically replace\n   `var/checkpoint.json`, then sync its directory. The checkpoint includes the\n   last processed ID, document count, completion flag, and shard byte lengths.\n3. On restart, truncate tails to those lengths and remove uncommitted shards\n   before resuming strictly **after** the last processed ID. SIGKILL during any\n   stage can leave replayable work, but cannot advance progress ahead of data.\n\nMissing/truncated committed shards are reported as storage damage rather than\nsilently skipped. Old checkpoints without shard lengths are not trustworthy\n(the old worker checkpointed buffered rows), so they trigger a one-time rebuild.\nThe document transform and JSONL row format are unchanged. This is a resumable\nfull backfill over a stable corpus, not an incremental change/deletion feed;\nuse `./jobs clean` to intentionally start a new full backfill after source changes.\nDo not clean a paused run if you want to preserve i"]
[167.590212, "i", "ts progress.\nEOF\n./jobs test > /tmp/reindex-tests-final.log 2>&1 &\n"]
