[167.63599, "o", "Keep invoking `./jobs reindex` until it exits 0 (75 means the supervised budget"]
[167.636106, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.636168, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> expired; committed work is safe). `./jobs status` reports checkpoint-certified\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[167.636268, "o", "rows, excluding any uncommitted tail. `./jobs history` records supervised runs."]
[167.636356, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.636418, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.63648, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.636609, "o", "> The usual budget, grace period, cooldown, and supervisor locking are unchanged."]
[167.636659, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.636694, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.63673, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.636779, "o", "> "]
[167.63683, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.636865, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.636918, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.637043, "o", "> Each batch (or partial batch on SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP) is committed in this order:"]
[167.637076, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.637157, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.637218, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.63728, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.637493, "o", "> "]
[167.642294, "o", "1. Flush rows, fsync **every** touched shard (including rotated ones), and sync"]
[167.642444, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.642884, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[167.642896, "o", "   the index directory."]
[167.643497, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.643704, "o", "> 2. Write the new checkpoint to a temporary file, fsync it, atomically replace"]
[167.643769, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.643806, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.643882, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.644016, "o", ">    `var/checkpoint.json`, then sync its directory. The checkpoint includes the"]
[167.644099, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.64422, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.644347, "o", "> "]
[167.644418, "o", "   last processed ID, document count, completion flag, and shard byte lengths."]
[167.644488, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.64456, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.644573, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.644689, "o", "> 3. On restart, truncate tails to those lengths and remove uncommitted shards"]
[167.644735, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.644778, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.644844, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.644954, "o", ">    before resuming strictly **after** the last processed ID. SIGKILL during any"]
[167.644999, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.645052, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.645104, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.645234, "o", ">    stage can leave replayable work, but cannot advance progress ahead of data."]
[167.645283, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.645338, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.645398, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.645446, "o", "> "]
[167.645465, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.645626, "o", "> Missing/truncated committed shards are reported as storage damage rather than"]
[167.645671, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.645722, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.645783, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.64589, "o", "> silently skipped. Old checkpoints without shard lengths are not trustworthy"]
[167.645935, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.646003, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.646056, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.646199, "o", "> (the old worker checkpointed buffered rows), so they trigger a one-time rebuild."]
[167.646245, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.646297, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.646369, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.646406, "o", "> "]
[167.646521, "o", "The document transform and JSONL row format are unchanged. This is a resumable"]
[167.64784, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.647862, "o", "> "]
[167.648018, "o", "full backfill over a stable corpus, not an incremental change/deletion feed;"]
[167.648062, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.648149, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.648288, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[167.648392, "o", "use `./jobs clean` to intentionally start a new full backfill after source changes."]
[167.648446, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.648454, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[167.648575, "o", "Do not clean a paused run if you want to preserve its progress."]
[167.648618, "o", "\r\n"]
[167.648673, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.648693, "o", "> "]
[167.64896, "o", "EOF"]
[167.648973, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[167.651845, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[167.652054, "o", "root@497dc6d7a000:/app# "]
